<mxfile host="Electron" agent="Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) draw.io/26.0.16 Chrome/132.0.6834.196 Electron/34.2.0 Safari/537.36" version="26.0.16">
  <diagram id="chartres" name="Chartres data request">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1136" dy="787" grid="1" gridSize="20" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1700" pageHeight="1200" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;b&gt;Chartres: data needed for the EU report (meeting reference, 2026-10-22)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Goal: compile the Chartres Excel files into the same 3 tables the other sites write to eu_report/report/&amp;lt;table&amp;gt;/site=Chartres/" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=16;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1560" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tables" value="&lt;b&gt;1. The 3 EU report tables (what Tableau reads)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellpadding=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Table&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;One row =&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Key columns&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Used for&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plan_OPT_EU&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;machine x day x shift x product&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Date, MachineName, ShiftName, PartName, Good Parts, Capacity,&lt;br&gt;Total Time, Planned OpT, OEE Time, Downtime Units,&lt;br&gt;OEE / PDT / UPDT Target, Dept, Area, Product Type&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Production and OEE&lt;br&gt;(core table, 9 visuals)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Time_Utilisation_EU&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;machine x day&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;OEE Time Total, Total Time Total, Planned OPT Total, All Time (1440)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Time split. Built from the same data&lt;br&gt;as Plan OPT: nothing extra needed&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Daily_Losses_EU&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;one stop&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Date, Time, MachineName, PartName, ShiftName, Group, SubGroup,&lt;br&gt;Desc, Duration, Comment, Equipment, Loss Units,&lt;br&gt;Value (loss target), Volume Total&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Loss analysis (6 visuals)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br&gt;Machine Names (Dept, Area, Product Type) is a lookup, not a table, but 13 of 16 visuals depend on it." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="90" width="1000" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ranking" value="&lt;b&gt;2. What to get from Chartres, most important first&lt;/b&gt; (cover 1 to 3 in the meeting, the rest by email)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellpadding=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;#&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Data&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Fields&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Fills&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Production&lt;/b&gt; per machine, day, shift, product&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;good parts, capacity (or design speed), total time,&lt;br&gt;planned operating time, OEE time, downtime&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Plan_OPT_EU + Time_Utilisation_EU&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Machine list&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;machine name, Dept, Area, Product Type&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;filters and grouping of every visual&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stop log&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;start time, machine, product, shift,&lt;br&gt;group (Planned / Unplanned / Not Logged),&lt;br&gt;sub group, description, duration, comment&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Daily_Losses_EU&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Targets (glidepaths)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;per line and month: OEE %, Planned DT %,&lt;br&gt;Unplanned DT %, target per loss bucket&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;target columns (else empty)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mappings to EU names&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;their shifts to Red / Green / Gold / Blue / Day / Night / Afternoon;&lt;br&gt;their loss sub groups to report buckets&lt;br&gt;(Adjustments, Breakdown, Minor Stops, Quality Issues, ...)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;ShiftName, SubGroup, loss targets&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;6&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Equipment coding&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;machine + description to equipment&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Equipment (no main-page visual)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br&gt;Not needed as a file: Loss Units and Volume Total (derived from capacity or speed x duration)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="420" width="1000" height="420" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="questions" value="&lt;b&gt;3. Questions for the meeting&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Where do the Excel files live (SharePoint site / folder)?&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Who updates them, and how often?&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Is the column layout fixed?&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;How much history do they have?&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;When does the production day start?&lt;br&gt;(time zone Europe/Paris, already supported in Config)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Can they export CSV instead of .xlsx?&lt;br&gt;(the flows read CSV; Machine Names .xlsx was converted by hand)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Is the data per machine or per line?&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;SIH already has 1 Chartres OEE line (asset list 2026-10-20):&lt;br&gt;which source is official for it, SIH or Excel?&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do they have a Provideam (or other MES) export behind the Excel?&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="90" width="520" height="420" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow" value="&lt;b&gt;How it lands in the report&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Chartres Excel / CSV&lt;br&gt;-&amp;gt; eu_report/pbi_report/source/&amp;lt;type&amp;gt;/site=Chartres/ (month files)&lt;br&gt;-&amp;gt; eu_report/reference/&amp;lt;type&amp;gt;/site=Chartres/ (machine names, glidepaths, ...)&lt;br&gt;-&amp;gt; PBI report listener picks up the change&lt;br&gt;-&amp;gt; PBI report build writes the 3 tables&lt;br&gt;-&amp;gt; eu_report/report/&amp;lt;table&amp;gt;/site=Chartres/ -&amp;gt; Tableau&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Also needed: Chartres in 1.1 CONFIG (sites, lines, reportSource)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="540" width="520" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sharepoint" value="&lt;b&gt;4. Getting the files from SharePoint: options&lt;/b&gt; (detail: powerbi-data-map.drawio, sheet &quot;Explanation Three options flow charts&quot;)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellpadding=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Option&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;How it works&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Reckitt must do&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Status&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. Power Automate push&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;A flow triggers when a file is added or changed in the SharePoint folder&lt;br&gt;and posts it to a VFC http in endpoint, or uploads it to the data lake&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;premium licence, build the flow&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;NOT TESTED: size (up to 6.5 MB), UTF-16 decoding, key&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Direct access (Graph API)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The VFC reads the folder through Microsoft Graph with an app registration&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;IT approval, folder permissions&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;NOT TESTED: can the VFC reach Microsoft hosts at all?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. Manual copy&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Download the files, run our normalizer and upload scripts to eu_report/&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;folder access only&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;TESTED&lt;/b&gt;: how Hull, Nottingham, Weinheim were loaded&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Recommendation:&lt;/b&gt; start Chartres on option 3 to get data now; raise option 1 in the meeting as the long-term route (it needs their IT and a licence). Once files are in the lake, the listener tab picks them up automatically." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="870" width="1560" height="260" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
